[B]About[/B]

This is an unofficial TWRP 3.1.1-0.3 build for the [B]LG Optimus L3 E400[/B] (e0, Qualcomm MSM7x27A, eMMC). It is built with the Omni 4.4 tree and uses the stock V10c kernel (Linux 2.6.38.6-perf). It is the recovery used to install [URL="https://xdaforums.com/t/rom-unofficial-2-3-7-cyanogenmod-7-for-lg-optimus-l3-e400.4806727/"]CyanogenMod 7 for the E400[/URL].

[COLOR="Red"][B]Only flash this on the LG E400. The recovery partition is mmcblk0p17; writing it to another device or partition can brick the phone.[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status[/B][/SIZE]

Build: [B]twrp-3.1.1-0.3-e400.img[/B] (6479872 bytes)

Tested on real hardware:

[LIST]
[*]Boots to recovery, with touchscreen
[*]ADB in recovery
[*]Installing a ROM ZIP from the internal storage (CyanogenMod 7 for the E400)
[*]Flashing the image with dd to mmcblk0p17 and booting it
[*][B]Not tested by me:[/B] backup and restore of every partition, and the external microSD
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Partition layout used[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]/recovery: mmcblk0p17
[*]/boot: mmcblk0p9
[*]/system: mmcblk0p14 (ext4)
[*]/cache: mmcblk0p16 (ext4)
[*]/data: mmcblk0p21 (ext4)
[*]/emmc (internal storage, vfat): mmcblk0p20
[*]/external_sd (microSD, vfat): mmcblk1p1
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]

[B]Before starting:[/B] back up your current recovery and copy the backup away from the phone.

[B]From a rooted system or from your current recovery (adb root):[/B]

[CODE]adb shell dd if=/dev/block/mmcblk0p17 of=/sdcard/recovery_backup.img bs=4096
adb push twrp-3.1.1-0.3-e400.img /sdcard/
adb shell md5sum /sdcard/twrp-3.1.1-0.3-e400.img
adb shell dd if=/sdcard/twrp-3.1.1-0.3-e400.img of=/dev/block/mmcblk0p17 bs=4096
adb shell sync
adb reboot recovery[/CODE]

The md5sum must match the one below before you write the partition.

To go back, write your backup to the same partition.

[SIZE="4"][B]Entering recovery[/B][/SIZE]

From Android:

[CODE]adb reboot recovery[/CODE]

